From: Galdrun Audio <firmware@galdrun.local>
Subject: [PATCH] bus: ti-sysc: balance reserved AM335x timer clocks on suspend

The AM33xx reservation change makes ti-sysc enable the system timers in
addition to timer-ti-dm-systimer. The permanent no-idle reference keeps
Timer2's functional clock on after the clockevent suspend callback drops
its own reference, preventing the PER domain from entering DeepSleep0.

Drop only ti-sysc's references during system suspend and restore them on
resume. Leave probe, runtime PM and the timer register configuration alone:
timer-ti-dm-systimer owns the active clocksource and clockevent registers.
Other SoCs and non-reserved peripherals retain their existing behavior.

--- a/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
@@ -1424,6 +1424,15 @@ static int __maybe_unused sysc_noirq_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	ddata = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	/* The systimer driver suspends its own clocks later in syscore. */
+	if (ddata->reserved && sysc_soc->soc == SOC_AM33) {
+		if (ddata->enabled) {
+			sysc_disable_main_clocks(ddata);
+			ddata->needs_resume = 1;
+		}
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (ddata->cfg.quirks & SYSC_QUIRK_NO_IDLE)
 		return 0;
 
@@ -1442,6 +1451,14 @@ static int __maybe_unused sysc_noirq_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 	ddata = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	if (ddata->reserved && sysc_soc->soc == SOC_AM33) {
+		if (ddata->needs_resume) {
+			error = sysc_enable_main_clocks(ddata);
+			ddata->needs_resume = 0;
+		}
+		return error;
+	}
+
 	if (ddata->cfg.quirks & SYSC_QUIRK_NO_IDLE)
 		return 0;
 
